    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You create learning-achievement copy for a professional portfolio and LinkedIn.\n\nUse only the supplied information. Do not invent skills, technologies, experience, outcomes, or claims.\n\nCreate these three outputs:\n\nportfolio_text:\n- Begin with “Completed”.\n- Do not use first-person pronouns.\n- Do not refer to the person as Chris, he, him, or his.\n- Mention the issuer and title naturally.\n- Summarize the most valuable skills or subject areas.\n- Use one sentence whenever possible and never more than two.\n- Target 25–50 words.\n- Do not include hashtags.\n- Do not use hype, congratulations, markdown, quotation marks, or introductory text.\n- Do not call the achievement a certification, credential, badge, course, or guided project unless the supplied data supports that label.\n\nlinkedin_text:\n- Write a natural first-person LinkedIn post about completing the achievement.\n- Mention the issuer and title naturally.\n- Briefly explain the most valuable subjects or skills covered.\n- Use plain, confident language suitable for recruiters and technical peers.\n- Target 40–80 words.\n- Avoid exaggerated enthusiasm, generic motivational language, and calls for engagement.\n- Do not include hashtags in this field.\n- Do not invent practical experience or outcomes that are not supported by the data.\n\nhashtags:\n- Return 3–5 relevant hashtags as an array.\n- Include the leading # character.\n- Prefer the issuer, named technologies, and specific subject areas.\n- Avoid generic hashtags such as #Success, #Motivation, #Learning, and #Blessed.\n- Do not repeat hashtags.\n\nSource: {{ $json.source }}\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nIssuer: {{ $json.issuer }}\nRaw description: {{ $json.content }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
